{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage","id":933985,"title":"Fixing Gurahl Rage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-19T11:13:42-07:00","id":933985,"title":"Fixing Gurahl Rage","content":"One of the problems with playing the Gurahl is that their Rage is so weak in comparison to the rest of the Changing Breeds (even the Nuwisha get a better rage if they take a level 3 Gift). While the ability to increase Health Levels for a scene is good, it is mechanically inferior to taking multiple actions. The ability to boost Stamina for one turn is not that useful and the ability to boost Strength is useless in the majority of forms because it is capped at twice human Strength.<br /> <br /> I suggest the following changes to make the Rage of the Gurahl comparable to the Rage of the other shapeshifter breeds. Gurahl may spend one point of Rage to increase their Strength, Stamina, or Health Levels by one for one scene. Strength and Stamina may not exceed twice the Strength or Stamina of the current form. Gurahl would retain their resistance to frenzy.<br /> <br /> I think that the change would allow the Gurahl to be the defenders and the protectors that they are thematically supposed to be without eliminating the differences that make them unique among the Changing Breeds. A Rage 10 Gurahl, which is a creature that is not nearly as dangerous to bystanders as a Rage 5 Garou, who possessed Strength 5 in Human form could transform into a Strength 10 Crinos and, over two turns, could spend 10 points of Rage to become Strength 20 for the remainder of the scene. A similar Gurahl who possessed Stamina 5 in Human form could transform into a Stamina 10 Crinos and, over two turns, could spend 10 points of Rage to become Stamina 20 for the remainder of the scene. Alternatively, either Gurahl could spend 10 point of Rage over two turns to gain ten extra health levels for a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T11:30:32-07:00","id":933993,"title":"","content":"I know I ended up changing Gurahl rage as well in a game a few years ago.<br /> <br /> I don't have my notes anywhere near me, but I want to say I had the Health levels stay the same (lasting for a scene and costing 1 for 1). Both Str and Stam changed to have no form based cap on raising them since that seemed arbitrary. Strength was raised by 2 per Rage spent, lasting for 1 turn. Stamina was raised 1 for 1, lasted a turn, but the extra stamina dots were treated as auto-soak against non silver damage.<br /> <br /> Honestly, changes help but when it comes down to it extra actions are just too good so there is very little that can be done to put Gurahl on par with the other changing breeds for Rage use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:01:05-07:00","id":934000,"title":"","content":"I do not know, but the ability to gain Strength 20 or Stamina 20 for a scene helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:18:43-07:00","id":934013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934000#post934000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know, but the ability to gain Strength 20 or Stamina 20 for a scene helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>And very possibly overpowered. Those stats are beyond Zmei and (most) Thunderwyrm levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:54:33-07:00","id":934036,"title":"","content":"What always irked me off, was that BTB the str increase was only for one round. NOT a full scene.<br /> So i made it go for 3 rounds if done on str. Alternately, each rage spent on Str (OR Stam) acts as one automatic success for THAT ROUND...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:20:17-07:00","id":934049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934036#post934036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What always irked me off, was that BTB the str increase was only for one round. NOT a full scene.<br /> So i made it go for 3 rounds if done on str. Alternately, each rage spent on Str (OR Stam) acts as one automatic success for THAT ROUND...</div> </div> </div> </div>how had that worked out for your games? Do you find that that solution was balanced? (insomuch as WoD games ever are)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:22:36-07:00","id":934051,"title":"","content":"Well, the Gurahl are supposed to be the most powerful of the Changing Breeds... Anyway, a properly designed Mokole can develop an Archid form with up to 19 Stamina and up to 29 damage dice for Body Slam and Overbear (and up to ten extra Health Levels), and they still get to have extra actions from spending Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:41:36-07:00","id":934061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934051#post934051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Gurahl are supposed to be the most powerful of the Changing Breeds... Anyway, a properly designed Mokole can develop an Archid form with up to 19 Stamina and up to 29 damage dice for Body Slam and Overbear (and up to ten extra Health Levels), and they still get to have extra actions from spending Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean about most powerful? I never noticed that anywhere...really strong sure...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:49:59-07:00","id":934066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934051#post934051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Gurahl are supposed to be the most powerful of the Changing Breeds... Anyway, a properly designed Mokole can develop an Archid form with up to 19 Stamina and up to 29 damage dice for Body Slam and Overbear (and up to ten extra Health Levels), and they still get to have extra actions from spending Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my point of view, when character ideas/concepts/etc start with &quot;a properly designed&quot; what follows is usually pointing out an example of a rules problem and not something that applies to the broader base of character ideas or supernatural creature types.<br /> Mokole Archid taints have their own inherent problems and are (conveniently) currently being discussed in another thread at the moment.<br /> <br /> I do completely agree that something needs to be done to buff Gurahl Rage expenditure. There just isn't going to be a definitive &quot;correct&quot; way to do it.<br /> <br /> I'm also not necessarily convinced that description-wise there is a difference between buffing health levels and buffing stamina, so there is that to consider. Mechanically they work very differently, but should have a better way to be represented in action. That's why I chose to have the Stamina be auto-soak. That way a Gurahl could (in theory) possibly stand up to a full round of attacks from a pack of Garou. But having said buff last longer than that runs the risk of having it be overpowered. A Gurahl with 20 stamina for a scene is nigh unkillable for an entire combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:52:10-07:00","id":934068,"title":"","content":"Well the real hell comes in as soon as someone starts handing out &quot;unsoakable&quot; in any sense. If someone can get multiple shots off on you in a round with silver, or some power, then that ends a Gurahl rather quickly, no matter how much stamina they get, and health levels drop pretty quickly in this sense. What if the Rage allowed them to effectively soak even the unsoakable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 07-19-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T14:10:37-07:00","id":934078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934068#post934068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the real hell comes in as soon as someone starts handing out &quot;unsoakable&quot; in any sense. If someone can get multiple shots off on you in a round with silver, or some power, then that ends a Gurahl rather quickly, no matter how much stamina they get, and health levels drop pretty quickly in this sense. What if the Rage allowed them to effectively soak even the unsoakable?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could also be interesting, though I would certainly limit it to a per round or per hit basis. Can't have an innate power like that <u>and</u> have it last any real length of time. <br /> <br /> Against unsoakable hits was the only time I ever really saw a benefit to spending Rage on health levels over stamina. And even then, the cost-benefit didn't seem wonderful. Especially compared to Garou, who should be using their equivalent Rage to dodge said attacks and thus avoid all damage. I do realize those are incredibly vague scenarios and that circumstances would change actions and reaction wildly, but they serve well enough for an example to balance against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T14:23:46-07:00","id":934087,"title":"","content":"Problem is, if you had that power only last for 1 round...its not much better then just tacking on health levels. You'd burn that Rage and then it'd be gone quickly (My group fought a Mokole once...one had a Klaive and made short order of the 60 ft mokole because his extra bruised levels disappeared quickly under the weight of unsoakable attacks....it took 2 hits...)It'd have to last at least a few rounds, it'd be for a roll kinda like Fortitude in vampire. Could stack with your stamina (for non-unsoakable rolls) or it could be used alone for the unsoakable (like silver, or Avatar of the Wyrm from the revised core). They are only dice so you do have a 50% of failure with each die you roll. I'd think having it last for a few rounds (like maybe your homid stamina in rounds) would be a fair way to compensate without giving them extra actions. To me it drives home the protector feel, but doesn't give them the feel I get from Garou for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T14:32:09-07:00","id":934097,"title":"","content":"Well, a combat optimized beginning Werewolf (which would be someone you would not want to be around under normal circumstances) in Crinos form would be capable of spending five points of Rage per turn to attack six times during the first turn and six times during the second turn. They will attack with 11 dice and deal 8 dice of aggravated damage. Assuming that the old rules concerning successes not adding to melee damage apply, they will deal an average of 4 health levels of aggravated damage per attack. They will do an average of 0.5 health levels of aggravated damage every attack to a similarly designed Gurahl, for three health levels of aggravated damage during the first turn and second turn. If the Gurahl spends five points of Rage per turn on extra health levels, since Rage points are spent before actions, the Gurahl would be able to survive to the third turn with four extra health levels for the remainder of the scene. <br /> <br /> The Gurahl will be able to attack with 9 dice each turn, dealing 9 dice of aggravated damage. They will do an average of 1 health level of aggravated damage every turn. If the Garou dodges once per turn during the first two turns and just attacks the following turns, it will take Gurahl eight turns to Incapacitated the Garou. The Gurahl has lost all of the extra health levels. Of course, everything changes with silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T14:57:35-07:00","id":934118,"title":"","content":"Also keep in mind that in W20 dodge is now a diff 5, vs claw attacks at diff 6 (or even soaking) at diff 6","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T15:22:00-07:00","id":934127,"title":"","content":"Yes, but the Gurahl is better off attacking each turn. Now, if the Garou is armed with a silver weapon...well, he has a bear skin rug after the first turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T15:42:42-07:00","id":934140,"title":"","content":"Eh, from experience (in at least 3 different games) Gurahl lose 100% of the time (against a similarly experienced Garou) with rules as written right now. So it's fairly obvious something needs doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe running it closer to Fortitude wouldn't be so bad. I might playtest that next time I run a game.<br /> I still like the idea of auto soak being mixed in. Maybe something like autosoak for bashing/lethal. Added soak (like normal stamina) for Agg and allows dice to soak for normally unsoakable damage (silver, as well as lethal or agg in breed forms). I do see the point of making it last more than a round. I'm just not sure about how that will work out balance-wise in game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T15:43:53-07:00","id":934144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934127#post934127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the Gurahl is better off attacking each turn. Now, if the Garou is armed with a silver weapon...well, he has a bear skin rug after the first turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea was that the Gurahl will never hit the Garou (or rarely will), so how much damage it can deal almost doesn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T16:46:43-07:00","id":934173,"title":"","content":"Well, mathematical, the Gurahl is better off until silver is introduced, then it is a turn one victory for the Garou. Ironically, the Swart are the best against the Garou when silver weapons are introduced because they have three higher Dexterity in Crinos form than Garou do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T17:35:25-07:00","id":934201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934144#post934144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the idea was that the Gurahl will never hit the Garou (or rarely will), so how much damage it can deal almost doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This was what I was getting at, yea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T19:48:01-07:00","id":934249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934173#post934173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, mathematical, the Gurahl is better off until silver is introduced, then it is a turn one victory for the Garou. Ironically, the Swart are the best against the Garou when silver weapons are introduced because they have three higher Dexterity in Crinos form than Garou do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Gurahl is better off mathematically...is altering anything really needed then?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T20:01:41-07:00","id":934252,"title":"","content":"Tanks gotta tank yo! Leave the dps to the wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T20:57:40-07:00","id":934268,"title":"","content":"Well, the problem is that Garou are going to have Klaives. Thematically, Garou were able to take out Gurahl because of pack tactics, not because of having an extra toy. Anyway, Bastet are better at DPS than Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:08:03-07:00","id":934272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934268#post934268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the problem is that Garou are going to have Klaives. Thematically, Garou were able to take out Gurahl because of pack tactics, not because of having an extra toy. Anyway, Bastet are better at DPS than Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know Klaives are supposed to be a rare fetish weapon that's only wielded by warriors of great renown, there isn't some caern out somewhere just mass producing them so they are standard issue equipment.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 07-20-2016, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:14:34-07:00","id":934273,"title":"","content":"Ok, let's also remember that the Garou ARE Gaia's warriors. Packs are a big advantage, but also don't knock a breed that is meant to be be war and war alone. Sure they have silver, they have packs, they have the Umbra. Can you have potent members of other breeds? Sure, but thematically I see nothing wrong with the warriors winning fights. By racking it up only to packs you're missing out on the &quot;warrior&quot; part of the theme. This is Werewolf the Apocalypse and not Animal Planet's Animal Face Off where we have wolves and bears actually fighting it out.<br /> <br /> On a side note, Shattered Dreams brings up the Garou won the War of Rage for many reasons aside from packs, and one of them is the use of silver. They adopted silver early in (Klaives, Silver Claws, Luna's Avenger), but they also used the Umbra as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 07-20-2016, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:48:01-07:00","id":934287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934273#post934273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is Werewolf the Apocalypse and not Animal Planet's Animal Face Off where we have wolves and bears actually fighting it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>For this line, I wish I could like this post more than once. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T22:02:04-07:00","id":934294,"title":"","content":"Rare is an interesting phenomena when you are talking about PCs. I think a fifth of my players have gotten around to creating their own Klaives, though they had Kinfolk do the silver forging. It started to be a rite of passage among my Ahroun players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T22:28:20-07:00","id":934302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934049#post934049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> how had that worked out for your games? Do you find that that solution was balanced? (insomuch as WoD games ever are)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. it used to be with the few players who DID opt for Gurahl, they would use rage for stamina or Health levels only. Now some actually do it for strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934061#post934061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean about most powerful? I never noticed that anywhere...really strong sure...</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC it was in the 2nd ed players guide which first said that the Garou are usually the most dexterous of the fera, but the Gurahl were the strongest..<br /> And the fact they get +5 to str vice +3 or +4 sure fits that mold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934066#post934066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934051#post934051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Gurahl are supposed to be the most powerful of the Changing Breeds... Anyway, a properly designed Mokole can develop an Archid form with up to 19 Stamina and up to 29 damage dice for Body Slam and Overbear (and up to ten extra Health Levels), and they still get to have extra actions from spending Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my point of view, when character ideas/concepts/etc start with &quot;a properly designed&quot; what follows is usually pointing out an example of a rules problem and not something that applies to the broader base of character ideas or supernatural creature types.<br /> Mokole Archid taints have their own inherent problems and are (conveniently) currently being discussed in another thread at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, its UP to the ST to approve any builds of pcs, especially with Mokole. I have certainly seen plenty cap Mokole players at 6 gnosis or there abouts, so they get no 4 slots huge size, terrible teeth, huge claws, tail, head spikes monstrosities..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934068#post934068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the real hell comes in as soon as someone starts handing out &quot;unsoakable&quot; in any sense. If someone can get multiple shots off on you in a round with silver, or some power, then that ends a Gurahl rather quickly, no matter how much stamina they get, and health levels drop pretty quickly in this sense. What if the Rage allowed them to effectively soak even the unsoakable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.. I like that Idea.. Each point of rage spent on Stamina, allows the Gurahl, to soak his HUMAN stamina rating + # of rage points spent, of normally unsoakable damage, but it lasts only for that combat round..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934087#post934087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is, if you had that power only last for 1 round...its not much better then just tacking on health levels. You'd burn that Rage and then it'd be gone quickly (My group fought a Mokole once...one had a Klaive and made short order of the 60 ft mokole because his extra bruised levels disappeared quickly under the weight of unsoakable attacks....it took 2 hits...)It'd have to last at least a few rounds, it'd be for a roll kinda like Fortitude in vampire. Could stack with your stamina (for non-unsoakable rolls) or it could be used alone for the unsoakable (like silver, or Avatar of the Wyrm from the revised core). They are only dice so you do have a 50% of failure with each die you roll. I'd think having it last for a few rounds (like maybe your homid stamina in rounds) would be a fair way to compensate without giving them extra actions. To me it drives home the protector feel, but doesn't give them the feel I get from Garou for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>How's about this as a compromise..<br /> When a Gurahl spends rage for Stamina, it not only boosts his total soak pool whether in homid, or crinos form, but ALSO gives him his Homid rating for soaking Silver (and other damage) for half his homid rating in rounds. Each additional point of rage spent this way can be either used to add ONE more dice to the soak total, OR to add one more round to the duration it lasts for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934173#post934173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, mathematical, the Gurahl is better off until silver is introduced, then it is a turn one victory for the Garou. Ironically, the Swart are the best against the Garou when silver weapons are introduced because they have three higher Dexterity in Crinos form than Garou do.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure. Lets take a beginning Garou, 4 str, 3 Dex, 3 stam, who's an Ahroun.. So he has 5 rage (NO freebies spent on these stuff).. Lets give him 3 dodge and 3 brawl.<br /> He's going one on one with a Gurahl, who has the exact same physical allocations and skills. HIS starting rage though is linked to his tribe. So we will say the one giving him 5 rage also.<br /> Both are fighting in Crinos form.<br /> So our Garou gains +4 str (putting him at 8), +1 Dex (putting him at 4) and +3 stam (putting him at 6). Adding in his skill value, he attacks at 7 and defends at 7. The garou spends ONE rage a round to give him 1 extra action (a dodge to his main action of attack). <br /> <br /> Our Gurahl though, gains +5 Str (placing him at 9), Loses 1 Dex (dropping him to 2), and +5 stam (putting him at 8). The Gurahl, lacking the capacity to do extra actions has to split his pool, so is rolling 2 for attack and 3 for defense.. (Using the 2e Revised rules on dice pool penalties for multiple actions here).. He spends one rage each round for an extra health level.<br /> <br /> So the Garou attacks first, with his 7 dice to hit, averaging 3.5 successes. The Gurahl though nets only one success on his dodge. So gets hit.. The Garou does 10d of damage (8 str +2 claws), so nets 5 damage. The Gurahl soaks 4 average from his 8 stamina. So nets one health level of damage. Since he has +1 health levels he has an extra bruise so far.<br /> Now comes the return attack. With only 2 dice to attack, the likelihood of the Gurahl hitting with the Garou having 7 dice to defend with is practically NIL.. So he has no real capacity to strike back.. <br /> This goes on that way for 5 rounds till the Garou is out of rage.. Then drops down to the Gurahl's way of needing to split dice.. BUT his 1 damage a round he has suffered has been effectively neutralized by his extra health levels.<br /> <br /> Now if on that 6th round the Garou decides to make an attack AND a dodge (well parry really), he attacks at 5 and dodges at 4. So now the Gurahl says &quot;Screw it&quot; and goes only with one action.. Attack. The Garou is certain to hit, dealing on average one additional health level, finally taking the LAST bruised level of the Gurahl. He counters and on average will connect on the garou.. His greater strength though, means he is rolling 11d for damage vs the 6d of the Garou for soaking.. On average that means the Gurahl is getting 5.5 damage, and the Garou only 3 soak for 2.5 wounds average.. Taking him down to between hurt and injured (-1d to all actions) in one blow..<br /> <br /> Now we get to round 7, where both combatants do the same. Garou finally knocks the Gurahl down to hurt (-1d to all actions), and his net average attack will still hit the net dodge average of the weakened garou.. So that 10 dice now of the gurahl's attack vs the 5 of the garou, gives another 2.5 wounds (average).. So he is now down 5 health levels...Which is at mauled (-2 dice).. Another hit and he's dead...<br /> <br /> So mathematically, if the Garou is alone, and can overwhelm the Gurahl early with popping all his rage off the bat to attack and weaken him down quickly, sure he's winning.. However if and ONLY if the Gurahl can survive till that point in time, that the garou is out of rage, he then can gain the upper hand.. And that's Only if he was smart to pump his extra health levels or stamina up to soak all that the Garou gave out..<br /> <br /> PS what did you mean by Swart?? The Swara (were cheetah??)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934268#post934268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the problem is that Garou are going to have Klaives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every Garou is gonna have a klaive.. and nothing says a Gurahl won't have something similar..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:32:03-07:00","id":934312,"title":"","content":"So... Dumb question:<br /> <br /> <b><i>WHY</i></b> do you have the Garou and the Gurahl fighting each other?<br /> <br /> I agree that if werewolves and werebears get into a fight, the bears (thematically -- as not being Gaia's warrior race) should get massacred. What I don't get is why you'd let the Garou get away with that in the first place. Thematically, the Garou going nuts and doing the whole War of Rage thing was largely what created much of the stuff that's wrong with the world in the modern nights. If I were the storyteller and the PC pack just mindlessly slaughtered a Gurahl (because he wasn't offering up the proper respect or they just didn't like him, or whatever), I'd nail the players by subsequently (and immediately thereafter) presenting them with a situation where the <b><i>ONLY</i></b> win would be with the aid of a Gurahl -- that now will not be there because they just pulped him for three points of temporary Glory.<br /> <br /> The Gurahl shouldn't be the same combat monsters that the Garou are. That's not their sacred role. The Garou are supposed to be<b><i> protecting </i></b>them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:38:25-07:00","id":934318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934051#post934051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Gurahl are supposed to be the most powerful of the Changing Breeds... Anyway, a properly designed Mokole can develop an Archid form with up to 19 Stamina and up to 29 damage dice for Body Slam and Overbear (and up to ten extra Health Levels), and they still get to have extra actions from spending Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Holding up the most broken possible combination of Mokole traits in the game (like seriously, there probably isn't even a single Mokole in the entire setting with the stats you just described) and using that as the baseline comparison for where you want every Gurahl to be seems like you are going to end up with Gurahl who are pretty overpowered in comparison to everyone else.<br /> <br /> I do think Gurahl are in need of a moderate buff, but allowing them to hit 20 Strength/Stamina for a scene seems pretty nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T00:02:00-07:00","id":934323,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that I addressed that during the W20 Open Development phase and that W20 Changing Breed reads:<br /> <span style=\"color:#DDA0DD\"><i>A Gurahl may also increase her Strength or Stamina by spending Rage on a one-for-one basis. She can raise her Strength to a maximum of twice her current form\u2019s Strength, and her Stamina to up to twice her current form\u2019s Stamina. Gurahl may combine increases in both Strength and Stamina by dividing up her expended Rage points between the two Attributes. Such increases in<br /> Strength and Stamina last for one turn per dot of Rage.</i></span><br /> <br /> The author saw, that one turn wasn't a suitable choice for the bonuses, but neither was a whole scene. So permanent Rage in turns seems to be a good fit. Caps are at double the current forms Strength/Stamina, so that isn't an issue either.<br /> <br /> As far as thematically comparing the combat prowess of Gurahl and Garou goes, it has to be said that thematically one has to compare A PACK of werewolves to a lone werebear. Because, well, that's how the whole thing works, thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:46:58-07:00","id":934368,"title":"","content":"There is a tweak that I use that helps out here. Allow use of Strength for attack rolls as long as they don't need particular finesse. It helps a lot. For the Gurahl, I went with scenelong increase for stamina and strength, and that made them pretty scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:38:01-07:00","id":934488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934323#post934323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to point out that I addressed that during the W20 Open Development phase and that W20 Changing Breed reads:<br /> <span style=\"color:#DDA0DD\"><i>A Gurahl may also increase her Strength or Stamina by spending Rage on a one-for-one basis. She can raise her Strength to a maximum of twice her current form\u2019s Strength, and her Stamina to up to twice her current form\u2019s Stamina. Gurahl may combine increases in both Strength and Stamina by dividing up her expended Rage points between the two Attributes. Such increases in<br /> Strength and Stamina last for one turn per dot of Rage.</i></span><br /> <br /> The author saw, that one turn wasn't a suitable choice for the bonuses, but neither was a whole scene. So permanent Rage in turns seems to be a good fit. Caps are at double the current forms Strength/Stamina, so that isn't an issue either.<br /> <br /> As far as thematically comparing the combat prowess of Gurahl and Garou goes, it has to be said that thematically one has to compare A PACK of werewolves to a lone werebear. Because, well, that's how the whole thing works, thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not mind that fix. A Rage 10 Gurahl could have Strength and Stamina bonuses that last the entire fight while a Rage 5 Gurahl has its edge for a while. I am quite willing to use that rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T13:19:05-07:00","id":934677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934312#post934312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Dumb question:<br /> <br /> <b><i>WHY</i></b> do you have the Garou and the Gurahl fighting each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, there's been 4 instances in game where as ST, the party fought Gurahl. Once was over a willful misunderstanding BY the pack alpha in what a Gurahl told them to do (repaying a favor his father owed the bear), which led them into a bad situation, so he could turn it around on the bear &quot;see it was HIS fault&quot;.. Luckly the pack stood by while their Alpha went one on one with the bear.. And lost Miserably (Rank 3 Gurahl NPC, Rank 2 garou).. needless to say he lost a boatload of renown, not only for his willful backstabbing, but his unworthy challenge.<br /> The 2nd i remember, was cause the pack wanted something they heard was in the bear's glade zone (in the real world portion), and rather negotiating, they said &quot;screw it lets take him out, and take it&quot;..<br /> I forget what caused the 3rd and 4th incidents, though i Do remember some of them.. One was a SWIFT victory for the party vs the lone Gurahl, while the other was against a mated pair (Male kin, female Gurahl). They had 3 of the pack almost dead from that battle..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934312#post934312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that if werewolves and werebears get into a fight, the bears (thematically -- as not being Gaia's warrior race) should get massacred. What I don't get is why you'd let the Garou get away with that in the first place. Thematically, the Garou going nuts and doing the whole War of Rage thing was largely what created much of the stuff that's wrong with the world in the modern nights. If I were the storyteller and the PC pack just mindlessly slaughtered a Gurahl (because he wasn't offering up the proper respect or they just didn't like him, or whatever), I'd nail the players by subsequently (and immediately thereafter) presenting them with a situation where the <b><i>ONLY</i></b> win would be with the aid of a Gurahl -- that now will not be there because they just pulped him for three points of temporary Glory.</div> </div> </div> </div>See above!..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934368#post934368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a tweak that I use that helps out here. Allow use of Strength for attack rolls as long as they don't need particular finesse. It helps a lot. For the Gurahl, I went with scenelong increase for stamina and strength, and that made them pretty scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good compromise.. Letting their Str substitute in place of Dex for attacking. Since they DO seem to be more HARD hitters than finess hitters.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T01:04:48-07:00","id":934954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933985-fixing-gurahl-rage?p=934677#post934677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good compromise.. Letting their Str substitute in place of Dex for attacking. Since they DO seem to be more HARD hitters than finess hitters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one caveat. Be aware that this makes the fights quite a bit deadlier and faster. The PC's will want to strike first, strike hard, because the fights will be over very quick and you'll either be victorious or very dead. It's done wonders for speeding up the fights.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T01:41:23-07:00","id":934962,"title":"","content":"As a way to make it less nasty. IF someone takes that option of using Str in place of Dex for attacking, their Brawl can't add more than their HOMID str rating to said attack roll.. <br /> Or go with, If they take this option, they can't defend... So no parry roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T05:51:58-07:00","id":935013,"title":"","content":"Hm, I think that Strength should be the best Attribute for Beats. A successful Beat would do no damage but would increase your die pool for the next attack by one per success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}